                      tree_sitter/alloc.h

Why generated: the published parser.c declares LANGUAGE_VERSION 15, and the
tree-sitter runtime bundled by smacker/go-tree-sitter accepts ABI 13-14 only
(api.h: TREE_SITTER_LANGUAGE_VERSION 14), so ts_parser_set_language would
reject it and Perl would silently fall back to the regex tier — the same wall
that forced the older pin in ../dart/binding.go. No ts-parser-perl release is
ABI 14 (checked 1.0.0 through 2.0.0), so parser.c is regenerated rather than
the grammar down-pinned:

  $ tree-sitter --version
  tree-sitter 0.23.2 (d97db6d63507eb62c536bcb2c4ac7d70c8ec665e)
  $ tree-sitter generate --abi 14 --no-bindings src/grammar.json

0.23.2 is the last release line that emits ABI 14. grammar.json is untouched
by the command (still byte-identical to the tag) and is vendored so the
regeneration is reproducible offline.

Verification of the regeneration (throwaway harness, not a committed test):
this parser and the previous grammar (ganezdragon/tree-sitter-perl 1.1.2, the
Rust engine's pin, regenerated at ABI 14 the same way) loaded side by side
under the smacker runtime and parsed 1,398 real-world Perl files (Mojolicious
9.39, DBIx-Class master, SpamAssassin master), counting files with no
ERROR/MISSING node:

  ganezdragon 1.1.2    :  800 failures   42.8% clean
  ts-parser-perl 2.0.0 :   11 failures   99.2% clean   (72.7x fewer failures)

which independently corroborates issue #61's 8,342-file benchmark
(40.2% vs 95.4%). The 11 remaining failures are the corpora's deliberate
syntax-error fixtures (t/lib/DBICTest/SyntaxErrorComponent{1,2,3}.pm,
t/mojo/lib/Mojo/Loader*Exception.pm, MojoliciousTest/SyntaxError.pm) and a few
preprocessor-shaped test files. The grammar's own 283-case upstream corpus
passes identically from the ABI-14 generation and from the published ABI-15
one (282/283 both, the same single "Double dollar edge cases" node-kind
difference), so regenerating introduces no behavioral change.

The Go tier under -tags tstree pins the extraction behavior on the fixtures in
../testdata/perl (TestExtractPerl, TestExtractPerlModernConstructs).
